.TH xil-remove-episode 1  "xil-remove-episode " 
.SH NAME
xil\-remove\-episode \- Remove all workspace files for a single episode. The source production script, masters/, and the sfx edit journal are never touched. Shared assets (SFX/, logs/) are never touched.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBxil\-remove\-episode\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-show\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITAG\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove all workspace files for a single episode. The source production script, masters/, and the sfx edit journal are never touched. Shared assets (SFX/, logs/) are never touched.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-show\fR \fI<SHOW>\fR
Show name or slug (default: resolved from project.json / XIL_PROJECTROOT)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be removed without deleting anything
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fITAG\fR>
Episode tag to remove (e.g. S01E01)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  xil remove\-episode S01E01 \-\-dry\-run
  xil remove\-episode S01E01 \-\-yes
  xil remove\-episode S01E01 \-\-show "Night Owls" \-\-dry\-run
